[{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5133062732","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121941#issuecomment-5133062732","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121941","id":5133062732,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMfRSTA","user":{"login":"dsnopek","id":191561,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE5MTU2MQ==","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/191561?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek","html_url":"https://github.com/dsnopek","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/dsnopek/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-30T15:44:28Z","updated_at":"2026-07-30T15:44:28Z","body":"I'm not really qualified to review this code, but the high-level idea makes sense to me!","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5133062732/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5140692664","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121941#issuecomment-5140692664","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121941","id":5140692664,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABMmi-uA","user":{"login":"smix8","id":52464204,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjUyNDY0MjA0","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52464204?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8","html_url":"https://github.com/smix8","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/smix8/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-07-31T08:01:08Z","updated_at":"2026-07-31T08:01:08Z","body":"Rendering is not the only one that is has a problem with an overtasked threadpool, it is just the one that is immediately noticeable because you cant really ignore the choppy visuals.\r\n\r\nThis change stagnates the rest of the thread pool and engine systems that also need thread. It prioritizes rendering like a bulldozer ignoring that now it extra starves others. Engine systems that when starved block the loop from even processing to reach rendering.\r\n\r\nSo it just shifts the blame and problem to others. Basically does what the cursed AudioServer does where the engine is starving due to occupied thread tasks but at least audio shows fake peak performance with its dedicated thread.\r\n\r\nThe actual engine solution would be that we allow major systems and servers that should not be fully staggered from too many started generic loader or script tasks (rendering, physics, nav ...) to reserve dedicated threads with a setting.\r\n\r\nWhen that setting is active it should also automatically reduce the generic threadpool thread count by that dedicated thread amount so the threadpool does not assume it has far more processing power available than what it actually can use. Stops it from starting too many tasks at once that then all slowly fight over non-existing actual threads.\r\n","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5140692664/reactions","total_count":1,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":1,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5182457353","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/121941#issuecomment-5182457353","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/121941","id":5182457353,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc8AAAABNOYGCQ","user":{"login":"clayjohn","id":16521339,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE2NTIxMzM5","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/16521339?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn","html_url":"https://github.com/clayjohn","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/clayjohn/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-08-04T17:28:35Z","updated_at":"2026-08-04T17:28:35Z","body":"> This change stagnates the rest of the thread pool and engine systems that also need thread. It prioritizes rendering like a bulldozer ignoring that now it extra starves others. Engine systems that when starved block the loop from even processing to reach rendering.\r\n\r\nHow does this starve anything? It is on a dedicated thread. It doesn't share resources with any other system","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/5182457353/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null}]